{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בפרך", :translit "b'farekh", :gloss "with crushing labor"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "בפרך", :expansion ["בפה" "רך"]}], :frame {:text "The word בפרך is read as a notarikon: בפה רך, 'with a soft mouth.' Pharaoh deceived Israel into forced labor by initially addressing them gently, saying he was recruiting them for a building project. Pharaoh himself worked alongside them at first to cement the ruse; once they were committed, the heavy yoke was imposed. This expansion as בפה רך is found in Sotah 11b and in the Mekhilta's comment on this phrase.", :sources ["Sotah 11b" "Mekhilta d'Rabbi Yishmael, Bo 1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "בפרך", :expansion ["בפה" "רך"], :initials ["ב" "ר"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:56.968290241Z", :model "glm-5.2"}